@startuml sequence_datastream
title DataStream frame submission and retrieval (shared memory)

skinparam shadowing false

participant "Producer\n(e.g. CameraService\nacquisition loop)" as Prod
participant "DataStream\n(producer side)" as DS1
participant "SharedMemory\n(header + ring buffer)" as SHM
participant "Event\n(futex / condvar /\nsemaphore / spinlock)" as Ev
participant "DataStream\n(consumer side)" as DS2
participant "Consumer\n(e.g. CameraProxy.\ntake_raw_exposures)" as Cons

== Setup ==
Prod -> DS1 : MakeDataStream("images",\ndtype, shape, num_frames)
DS1 -> SHM : Create(stream_id, header +\nnum_frames * frame_size)
DS1 -> Ev : Create(shared event)

Cons -> DS2 : GetDataStream("images")
DS2 -> SHM : Open(stream_id)\n(map same memory)
DS2 -> Ev : Open(same event)

== Produce a frame ==
loop acquisition loop
    Prod -> DS1 : RequestNewFrame()
    DS1 -> SHM : reserve slot\n(next_request_id % num_frames)
    DS1 --> Prod : DataFrame (view into buffer)
    Prod -> SHM : write pixel data\n(C-contiguous, matching dtype/shape)
    Prod -> DS1 : SubmitFrame(frame.id)
    DS1 -> SHM : atomically update\nm_LastId, timestamp
    DS1 -> Ev : Signal()
end

== Consume frames ==
Cons -> DS2 : GetNextFrame(timeout_ms)
alt frame already available
    DS2 -> SHM : check m_FirstId <= id <= m_LastId
    DS2 --> Cons : DataFrame (zero-copy view)
else frame not yet submitted
    DS2 -> Ev : Wait(timeout_ms,\ncondition = IsFrameAvailable(id))
    Ev --> DS2 : woken by producer Signal()
    DS2 --> Cons : DataFrame
end
Cons -> Cons : frame.data.copy()\n(copy before next overwrite\nif data is kept)

note over SHM
  Ring buffer semantics: frame ids increase
  monotonically; slot = id % num_frames.
  Old frames are overwritten, so consumers
  must copy data they want to keep.
end note

note over DS2, Cons
  GetLatestFrame() returns the newest frame
  without waiting. Waits are specified
  in milliseconds in the Python API.
end note

@enduml
